  "description": "Founded in 1911, the University of Regina is a public research university located in the Canadian province of Saskatchewan. The University of Regina campus is home to 10 faculties, 25 academic departments and schools, 18 research centers and institutes, and three unified colleges. We offer more than 120 undergraduate and 78 graduate programs, including many specialized programs such as police science and public policy. The University of Regina promises staff, faculty, and students success in a superior environment.\n\nHere are some of the popular undergraduate and graduate programs the University of Regina offers.\n\nThe University of Regina provides students with accommodation services on and off campus. The University has fully furnished rooms ranging from dormitories to 6 bedroom apartments, These dormitories consist of five dormitory buildings Paskwaw and Wakpa Towers, Kisik Towers, Luther College, La Cite and College West. With its views, spacious rooms, and campus security, the dormitory building experience offers students a different experience.\n\nAdditionally, the University of Regina offers off-campus accommodation in the form of private apartments and homestay options. Off-campus residences are also affordable and range from CAD 674 to CAD 1,260.",
